    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="0837" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/855</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2967</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 31, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 17</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my cablegram No. 3668 of the
                    29th instant in regard to the shipment of two cargoes of dyestuffs of German
                    origin to the United States,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d716-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith to the Department a copy of the note, dated the 28th instant,
                    which has been received from the Foreign Office in reply to the representations
                    of the Embassy in this connection, and in which it is set forth that if the
                    cotton which was shipped to Germany has been paid for in the United States in
                    cash, the British Government would raise no objection to a similar payment being
                    made in Germany for the two cargoes of dyestuffs.</p>
                <p>It is further stated that the permit would be issued in favor of the Republic
                    Trading Corporation instead of Mr. Mitchell.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Hines Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d716-a1.xml" xpointer="d716-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
